After studying at Meiji University, he worked at an office supplies company for a year while focusing on his passion for drawing. His manga The World is Mine was chosen by the editors of Pulp for their Manga Hell list of controversial manga. He is married to the mangaka [Kiwa Irie](https://anilist.co/staff/149869/Kiwa-Irie).', 'gender': 'Male', 'age': 63, 'primaryOccupations': ['Mangaka'], 'languageV2': 'Japanese'}}, {'role': 'Translator (French)', 'node': {'id': 226523, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n226523-5yDZX3EDfa2r.jpg'}, 'name': {'full': 'Patrick Honnoré'}, 'description': "Patrick Honnoré is a translator. He studied modern literature at the University of Provence in France and received an MA in 1988. After that he came to Japan to study comparative sociology at the University of Tokyo. After working for private companies and the Embassy of Haiti, he is now engaged in translating Japanese fiction into French as a freelance translator. He has translated Dogra Magra by Kyusaku Yumeno, Histoired'un squelette by Eiki Matayoshi and God's Boat by Kaori Ekuni for JLPP.

(Source: JLPP)", 'gender': None, 'age': None, 'primaryOccupations': ['Translator'], 'languageV2': 'French'}}]}

