Thriving on doing a bit of everything, Abigail has been working in the US manga industry since 2008. Since leaving her in-house editorial role in 2013, Abigail has undertaken a wide range of freelance assignments including editing and localizing translated scripts; lettering and retouching for manga interiors; and designing promotional items, ads, and cover logos.
When she isn't panels-deep in a new manga project, Abigail enjoys various other creative pursuits, as well as generally being out of doors.", 'gender': 'Female', 'age': None, 'primaryOccupations': ['Letterer'], 'languageV2': 'English'}}, {'role': 'Translator (Polish)', 'node': {'id': 354458, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n354458-49pu0BJ2ndi0.jpg'}, 'name': {'full': 'Adrianna Jarzębowska'}, 'description': '[Linkedin](https://www.linkedin.com/in/adrianna-jarz%C4%99bowska/)', 'gender': 'Female', 'age': None, 'primaryOccupations': ['Translator'], 'languageV2': 'Polish'}}, {'role': 'Art (chs 180-200)', 'node': {'id': 410229, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/default.jpg'}, 'name': {'full': 'DISCIPLES'}, 'description': 'A team of artists who worked with Seong-Rak Jang (DUBU). Solely created to produce side stories for Solo Leveling.', 'gender': None, 'age': None, 'primaryOccupations': [], 'languageV2': 'Korean'}}]}

