{'edges': [{'role': 'Story & Art', 'node': {'id': 110753, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n110753-MBFVFP7mwF3b.jpg'}, 'name': {'full': 'Sui Ishida'}, 'description': '[Main Twitter](https://twitter.com/sotonami) | [Secondary Twitter](https://twitter.com/sotonamix) | [YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCefY-So0u9tiqwCL1Xw3zvA/) | [Tumblr](https://sui-zakki.tumblr.com/) | [Instagram 1](https://www.instagram.com/ishida_____sui/) | [Instagram 2](https://www.instagram.com/ishida_sui/)

Sui Ishida, alternatively known as Sotonami, is a Japanese manga artist. He is best known for his dark fantasy series Tokyo Ghoul, a story about a young man named Ken Kaneki who gets transformed into a ghoul after encountering one. Additionally, he is the character designer and scenario writer for the Switch game Jack Jeanne.

He is also the younger brother of the novel writer [Shin Towada](https://anilist.co/staff/119987).', 'gender': 'Male', 'age': 39, 'primaryOccupations': ['Mangaka'], 'languageV2': 'Japanese'}}, {'role': 'Translator (Portuguese)', 'node': {'id': 227108, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n227108-eGXkRMagWPBV.png'}, 'name': {'full': 'Fernando Mucioli'}, 'description': '[Twitter](https://twitter.com/tengumaru)', 'gender': 'Male', 'age': None, 'primaryOccupations': ['Voice Actor'], 'languageV2': 'Portuguese'}}, {'role': 'Translator (Spanish)', 'node': {'id': 152615, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n152615-xt1M6jIT24Cw.jpg'}, 'name': {'full': 'Edith  Belarra'}, 'description': 'Edith Belarra was born in Huesca, Spain and licensed in Translation and Interpretation in the Universidad Autónoma de Barcelona, where she specialized in videogames. Her works consist mainly in translating from Japanese and English to Spanish.', 'gender': 'Female', 'age': None, 'primaryOccupations': ['Translator'], 'languageV2': 'Spanish'}}, {'role': 'Translator (French)', 'node': {'id': 230705, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/default.jpg'}, 'name': {'full': 'Akiko Indei'}, 'description': None, 'gender': None, 'age': None, 'primaryOccupations': ['Translator'], 'languageV2': 'French'}}, {'role': 'Translator (Korean)', 'node': {'id': 262203, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/default.jpg'}, 'name': {'full': 'Dong-Uk Kang'}, 'description': None, 'gender': None, 'age': None, 'primaryOccupations': ['Translator'], 'languageV2': 'Korean'}}, {'role': 'Translator (Polish)', 'node': {'id': 271831, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/default.jpg'}, 'name': {'full': 'Karolina Dwornik'}, 'description': None, 'gender': 'Female', 'age': None, 'primaryOccupations': ['Translator'], 'languageV2': 'Polish'}}, {'role': 'Translator (Chinese)', 'node': {'id': 337757, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/default.jpg'}, 'name': {'full': 'Siyu Lai'}, 'description': None, 'gender': None, 'age': None, 'primaryOccupations': ['Translator'], 'languageV2': 'Chinese'}}]}

characters:
{'edges': [{'voiceActors': [], 'node': {'id': 17606, 'name': {'full': 'Rock Holmes'}, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b17606-YeYdW2Qnhm0q.png'}, 'description': 'Rock is a recurrent character in Osamu Tezuka's manga series, and he is an important part of Osamu Tezuka's Star System. Rock is a young boy with shiny dark hair. He first appeared in the manga series Detective Boy Rock Holmes, as a child detective. While most of other Tezuka child characters stayed the same age, Rock grew up throughout the years and his character was reused for more mature "roles" in Tezuka's manga, where he gradually developed a darker personality.

Often cold and brutal, his character tends to be used as an antagonist, who later, in works such as Phoenix, kidnapped and murdered people. In this older form, Rock is often wearing a three-piece suit, a striped tie and dark sunglasses, the last of which became something of a trademark for him.

Best known to American audiences for his dark and violent roles in the Metropolis movie and second volume of Alabaster, Rock is sometimes good, sometimes evil, but always determined, absolute and charismatic.', 'gender': 'Male', 'age': None}}, {'voiceActors': [], 'node': {'id': 38754, 'name': {'full': 'Hi no Tori'}, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b38754-I7SNWHqNomgx.png'}, 'description': None, 'gender': None, 'age': None}}, {'voiceActors': [], 'node': {'id': 205901, 'name': {'full': 'Gaou'}, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b205901-EAWv0TpfMz4a.jpg'}, 'description': 'One-eyed and one-armed young man Gao, an ancestor of Saruta, turns into a murderous bandit when he is rejected by his village.', 'gender': 'Male', 'age': None}}, {'voiceActors': [], 'node': {'id': 32593, 'name': {'full': 'Dr. Saruta'}, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/32593.jpg'}, 'description': 'Like Dr. Ochanomizu, Saruta is visually identifiable by his large nose, though in his case it is grotesquely spotted. Where Ochanomizu generally appears in light and uplifting roles, Saruta is quite the opposite. His two main roles in Tezuka manga are both in extremely important series: Black Jack and Phoenix. In Phoenix, he is arguably an over-arching protagonist for the series as a whole, alongside its title character. He appears in every story, sometimes in a main role, sometimes in a peripheral one, sometimes with a new name and barely recognizable in his character, but always present and important. He is also distinguishable by the sheer amount of suffering he undergoes over the course of his many lives and deaths, as he demonstrates both the darker sides of human nature and the human capacity for perserverance and transcendence.  In Black Jack, he is featured as Dr. Honma Jotaro, once a skilled and famous surgeon later thrown out of the medical community due to jealousy and doubt about his research, who saved young Black Jack as a child, was Black Jack&#039;s principle father figure during his life, and inspired him to become a doctor. Since Saruta is the character in Phoenix who best understands the system of reincarnation, life and death, it is appropriate that in Black Jack Dr. Honma is the figure who most frequently reminds Black Jack about the power of nature and the inevitability of death.      (Source: tezukainenglish.com)', 'gender': 'Male', 'age': None}}, {'voiceActors': [], 'node': {'id': 231361, 'name': {'full': 'Masato Yamanobe'}, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b231361-160rHAJYIuXV.png'}, 'description': None, 'gender': None, 'age': None}}]}

staff:
{'edges': [{'role': 'Story & Art', 'node': {'id': 97539, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/2539.jpg'}, 'name': {'full': 'Nobuyuki Fukumoto'}, 'description': '[Twitter](https://twitter.com/fukumoto_pro)

Nobuyuki Fukumoto is a Japanese manga artist well known throughout the Far East for his unique original gambling ideas, deep psychological analysis of characters and distinct artstyle. Yakuza and gambling are recurring themes in his manga.

In English language countries, he is most famous as the author of Akagi, a mahjong-related manga. In 1998, he won the Kodansha Manga Award for Tobaku Mokushiroku Kaiji. An onomatopoeia "zawa" (ざわ‥), meaning uneasy atmosphere, appears frequently in his comics and is considered Fukumoto's trademark.', 'gender': 'Male', 'age': 67, 'primaryOccupations': ['Mangaka'], 'languageV2': 'Japanese'}}]}

characters:
{'edges': [{'voiceActors': [], 'node': {'id': 174319, 'name': {'full': 'Yu'}, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b174319-YCsHl8DS97Vt.jpg'}, 'description': "Yu is the main character of The Boxer. He becomes a professional boxer under the tutelage of the legendary [K](https://anilist.co/character/208937/K).

Yu has a very dark and melancholic appearance, with unstyled jet-black hair that drapes down loosely on his head, distinctively coal-black eyes with even darker pupils and a wholly disinterested facial expression painted on his face with an equally 'dead' look in his eyes. He has a very skinny body which belies his deceptively athletic abilities.

Yu has a startlingly emotionless and disinterested persona, taking little to no interest in anything other than his pet cat. He is shown to be alarmingly apathetic, simply taking hits because he couldn't be bothered to dodge them and giving zero response when threatened by an obviously vicious person.", 'gender': 'Male', 'age': '17-19'}}, {'voiceActors': [], 'node': {'id': 208938, 'name': {'full': 'Yuto Takeda'}, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b208938-rBloM9yDWzLh.jpg'}, 'description': "Yuto is known as a positive person, always looking at the bright side. He's very motivated and doesn't give up despite all the obstacles he had faced. He's motivating not only himself but also those around him, helping them at the same time.", 'gender': 'Male', 'age': None}}, {'voiceActors': [], 'node': {'id': 278944, 'name': {'full': 'J'}, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b278944-7sGg2scu5N5h.png'}, 'description': None, 'gender': 'Male', 'age': None}}, {'voiceActors': [], 'node': {'id': 208935, 'name': {'full': 'Jean-Pierre Manuel'}, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b208935-qNT5TKiqDaF6.png'}, 'description': 'Jean-Pierre Manuel (쟝 삐에르 마뉘엘, Jyang Ppieleu Manwiel) is a professional boxer and the former boxing lightweight world champion.', 'gender': None, 'age': None}}, {'voiceActors': [], 'node': {'id': 174317, 'name': {'full': 'Jay'}, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b174317-JBxQK6xceRk2.png'}, 'description': None, 'gender': None, 'age': None}}, {'voiceActors': [], 'node': {'id': 209085, 'name': {'full': 'Carmen'}, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b209085-5DXGNWyvdC5C.png'}, 'description': "She was hired as Yu's bodyguard before his fight with Santorino, she is also K's assistant.", 'gender': None, 'age': None}}, {'voiceActors': [], 'node': {'id': 208937, 'name': {'full': 'K'}, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b208937-9C9FSDMVXiga.jpg'}, 'description': 'He is a legendary boxing trainer, having raised 5 boxing world champions. He is currently training Yu.', 'gender': 'Male', 'age': None}}, {'voiceActors': [], 'node': {'id': 231926, 'name': {'full': 'Aaron Tide'}, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b231926-cCm6FbemP5vq.png'}, 'description': 'Aaron Tide is the Heavy Weight World Champion. He was trained under Coach K but currently fights under a different gym.', 'gender': 'Male', 'age': None}}, {'voiceActors': [], 'node': {'id': 174318, 'name': {'full': 'Baek-San Ryu '}, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b174318-nouM12QpelcH.png'}, 'description': None, 'gender': 'Male', 'age': None}}, {'voiceActors': [], 'node': {'id': 209083, 'name': {'full': 'Fabrizo Santorino'}, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b209083-N4b4RLiCaRx8.png'}, 'description': 'Santorino Fabrizo bears the title of Middle Weight Champion. He is famous for using tricky moves and cheats.', 'gender': 'Male', 'age': None}}, {'voiceActors': [], 'node': {'id': 231928, 'name': {'full': 'Marco Santorino'}, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b231928-5gR176EgOlzp.png'}, 'description': "Marco Santorino is [Fabrizio Santorino](https://anilist.co/character/209083/)'s older brother as well as coach. He is known for his dirty fighting tactics.", 'gender': 'Male', 'age': None}}, {'voiceActors': [], 'node': {'id': 231927, 'name': {'full': 'Viktor Grigoryevich'}, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b231927-xCRSPpNVdDcf.png'}, 'description': 'Viktor Grigoryevich is the current Cruiser Weight World Champion.', 'gender': 'Male', 'age': None}}, {'voiceActors': [], 'node': {'id': 208933, 'name': {'full': 'Misaki'}, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b208933-PKBykABskMpg.png'}, 'description': 'Misaki (미사키, Misaki) is the boxing coach of current light welterweight world champion Takeda Yuto.', 'gender': None, 'age': None}}, {'voiceActors': [], 'node': {'id': 208934, 'name': {'full': 'John Taker'}, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b208934-uS45ggBzqRIK.png'}, 'description': 'John puts on a decidedly confident and somewhat cocky air in public, with a great enjoyment in taking down talented young boxers with promising careers. To this end, he believes that bending the rules is more than okay if it leads to winning in the end.[1] He looks up to the middleweight champion boxer, Santorino Fabrizo, calling the man a true warrior on another level and saying he deserves more respect from people.', 'gender': None, 'age': None}}, {'voiceActors': [], 'node': {'id': 278941, 'name': {'full': 'Gilbert Einstein'}, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b278941-wlgXILA4osFt.png'}, 'description': 'Previous Cruiserweight World Champion before Viktor Grigorievich.', 'gender': 'Male', 'age': None}}, {'voiceActors': [], 'node': {'id': 208936, 'name': {'full': 'Kasim Al-Hajad'}, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b208936-KCGZu7rt2M3y.png'}, 'description': "Kasim is a swaggering, spoilt, and arrogant man with an extravagant showboating personality in and out of the ring, bringing about controversy and polarization in the Boxing world by merely participating. At any recourse, Kasim's first course of action is to try to throw money at the problem, paying people to spar with him and proposing to simply buy out the Boxing organization he competed in to change the rules to allow for illegal moves he performed out of ignorance.", 'gender': None, 'age': None}}, {'voiceActors': [], 'node': {'id': 208939, 'name': {'full': 'Josh'}, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b208939-1GVuBOPQjR1G.png'}, 'description': 'Josh (조시, Josi) was once a member of the Lions Boxing Club with dreams of becoming a professional boxer. However, after being annihilated by Yu, Josh gave up on his dream and currently works as a bartender.', 'gender': None, 'age': None}}, {'voiceActors': [], 'node': {'id': 328678, 'name': {'full': 'Siha Lee'}, 'image': {'large': 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b328678-hHPLKRNG2FYT.jpg'}, 'description': 'Siha Lee is a character in The Boxer universe. He was a boxing prodigy who was able to become one of the best boxers in Korea across all weight classes, being undefeated for 9 matches straight, with many top-ranking boxers unable to do anything against him, all of them suffering a crushing defeat by his hands. He was praised for his ability to memorize attack patterns, rhythms, timing, and everything about his opponents in a single round, using it all against them in the second round.', 'gender': 'Male', 'age': '22'}}]}

